    "category": "cyber",
    "topic": "Evidence Analysis",
    "question": "What do you do when telemetry sources disagree?",
    "answer": "I treat the disagreement as an investigative lead. I check time synchronization, collection gaps, field meaning, sensor scope, retention, and whether the products observed different stages of the event. I build a timeline from the highest-confidence artifacts, state the uncertainty, and avoid forcing a conclusion until the conflicting evidence is explained.",
