    "topic": "Containment",
    "question": "When would you isolate an endpoint instead of blocking an IP address?",
    "answer": "I isolate the endpoint when the host itself may be compromised, the behavior uses changing infrastructure, or continued internal access creates lateral-movement risk. I block an IP when the indicator is sufficiently reliable and the control will meaningfully reduce exposure without unacceptable business impact. Often both are useful, but containment must match the evidence and authorization.",
