    "topic": "Portfolio Conversation",
    "question": "You mention CrowdStrike. What have you done with it?",
    "answer": "A major focus of my CrowdStrike work has been understanding endpoint investigations rather than simply reacting to the detection name.\n\nI have worked through true-positive and false-positive investigation scenarios where the goal is to correlate endpoint behavior with supporting network and security telemetry.\n\nI look at process trees, execution context, command lines, persistence, network connections, DNS activity, affected users, and related indicators.\n\nThe decision point is important to me. I want to be able to explain why I would isolate a system, why I would not isolate it, what additional evidence I need, and whether the detection itself should be tuned.",
