    "answer": "With Microsoft security scenarios, I think in terms of an integrated investigation rather than Sentinel operating by itself.\n\nSentinel gives me the correlation and incident-management layer. Defender gives me endpoint evidence and containment capabilities. Entra ID gives me authentication, identity, session, and account context. Then I correlate DNS, network, firewall, and other telemetry to determine scope.\n\nMy sequence is detection, validation, scope determination, containment, eradication or recovery, and then lessons learned.\n\nI also think about what detection logic should have identified the activity earlier and whether the analytics rule, correlation logic, watchlist, automation, or playbook should be changed afterward.",
