    "question": "You have detection engineering projects too. What does that mean to you?",
    "answer": "Detection engineering is more than writing a query that finds something.\n\nI start with the behavior I am trying to detect and the telemetry required to observe it. Then I think about attacker behavior, ATT&CK techniques, expected legitimate behavior, exclusions, time windows, thresholds, and how the detection will behave in a real SOC.\n\nA detection that generates hundreds of meaningless alerts is not necessarily a good detection.\n\nI want detections that provide useful investigative context and can be tuned based on evidence without accidentally creating blind spots.",
