    "answer": "The project simulates a service-provider environment with ten network roles.\n\nI incorporated OSPF for internal routing, BFD for rapid failure detection, MPLS and LDP for label distribution, MP-BGP for VPN route exchange, VRFs for customer segmentation, routing policies, firewall controls, monitoring, SIEM integration, and Python-based health analysis.\n\nI then created operational scenarios rather than leaving it as a static topology.\n\nThose scenarios include normal operation, DDoS activity, an endpoint compromise, a routing failure, and route leakage.\n\nThe idea was to practice identifying whether a problem is operational, security-related, or both.",
