    "topic": "Portfolio Conversation",
    "question": "What would you do if ransomware was detected?",
    "answer": "My priority would be stopping the attack before additional systems are affected.\n\nI would isolate confirmed compromised endpoints, preserve relevant evidence, investigate the execution chain, identify the initial access vector, look for credential compromise, persistence, lateral movement, remote execution, and additional affected systems.\n\nI would block confirmed malicious infrastructure and reset or disable compromised credentials where necessary.\n\nI would also search for ransomware precursors across the environment rather than only looking for the final encryption event.\n\nRecovery would come from isolated, validated backups after the compromise had been contained and the root cause addressed.\n\nAfterward, I would improve detections for whatever stages we could have identified earlier.",
