    "id": "portfolio-019",
    "category": "portfolio",
    "topic": "Portfolio Conversation",
    "question": "What do you mean by threat hunting?",
    "answer": "For me, threat hunting begins with a hypothesis rather than waiting for a predefined alert.\n\nI might start with a behavior such as suspicious PowerShell execution, unusual DNS activity, credential misuse, rare outbound connections, or lateral movement.\n\nThen I identify the telemetry that could confirm or reject that hypothesis and pivot across endpoints, users, IP addresses, domains, processes, and time ranges.\n\nIf I find something meaningful, I continue expanding the scope until I understand the behavior.\n\nEven when the hunt finds nothing malicious, it can expose telemetry gaps or opportunities for new detections.",
